===Etymology===
Etymology unclear. Compare {{cog|lv|atā}}.<ref name=kalbosnamai>{{cite-web|title=Atia ar ate?|titleurl=http://www.kalbosnamai.lt/index.php?option=com_joomlaboard&Itemid=59&func=view&id=135&catid=2|site=kalbosnamai.lt|year=2010|publisher=[[:w:Institute of the Lithuanian Language|LKI]]|author=[[:lt:Rita Miliūnaitė|Rita Miliūnaitė]]}}</ref> The word may not be very old, and may ultimately derive from {{der|lt|fr|adieu}}, via a {{der|lt|sla}} intermediary.<ref name=vlkk>{{R:lt:VLKK|3952-atia-ate|atia, ate}}</ref>

===Interjection===
{{head|lt|interjection}}

# {{lb|lt|informal}} [[goodbye]], [[ta-ta]]
